# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# NOOL Frontend — Environment Variables Template
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Copy to `.env.local` (auto-gitignored) for local overrides, or set as real
# env vars on your hosting platform for production.
#
# Vite only exposes vars prefixed with `VITE_` to client code.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Backend API URL (production) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Required when the SPA is deployed to a different origin than the API.
# Leave blank locally — the Vite dev server proxies /api to BACKEND_TARGET.
#
# Example for production: https://api.nool.example.com/api
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# ── Dev proxy target (not exposed to client) ──────────────────────────────
# Where the Vite dev server forwards "/api/*" requests. Useful when running
# the backend on a different port or host during local development.
BACKEND_TARGET=http://localhost:8083
